    "created_at": "2026-10-26T19:46:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-26T19:50:06Z",
    "body": "> But are implementations performing the behavior specified for not throwing? Or are they just silently eating the exceptions? I would expect us to not send ill-formed XML across the network.\r\n\r\nThis is my interpretation, but maybe I am misunderstanding something from that commit and linked issue / corresponding tests. The WPT PR https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/5123 for 59c9cd9ae31fc8fafd1c327f2d2a1ca1e88da28f seems to test this behaviour, which all engines pass (now under https://wpt.fyi/results/xhr/send-entity-body-document-bogus.htm?label=experimental&label=master&aligned).\r\n\r\nI'm going off of tests here, so there's always the possibility of misinterpreting the results where implementation behaviour is more complex than I realise (like I managed in https://github.com/whatwg/xhr/issues/242#issuecomment-6396472226 😅) Not 100% sure what silently eating the exception means, is that not sending anything at all?",
